{% if slide_title %}
SLIDE OBJECTIVE: {{ slide_title }}
{% if core_hook %}
DECK NARRATIVE: {{ core_hook }}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
OBJECTIVE: {{ objective }}
{% endif %}
{% if slide_type %}
SLIDE TYPE: {{ slide_type }}
{% endif %}

COMPONENTS (put every one on the slide — each carries its own data):
{% for comp in components %}
- {{ comp.kind }}{% if comp.component_id %} [{{ comp.component_id }}]{% endif %}{% if comp.count > 1 %} (x{{ comp.count }}){% endif %}{% if comp.chart_type %} [{{ comp.chart_type }}]{% endif %}{% if comp.content_summary %}: {{ comp.content_summary }}{% endif %}
{% if comp.weight and comp.weight != "peer" %}  height-weight: {{ comp.weight }} (see WEIGHT ALLOCATION in layout grammar)
{% endif %}
{% if comp.design_hint %}  visual-intent: {{ comp.design_hint }}
{% endif %}
{% if comp.content_data %}
  Data for {{ comp.component_id or comp.kind }}:
  {% for key, value in comp.content_data.items() %}
  {{ key }}: {{ value }}
  {% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
DENSITY: {{ density }} | FONT TIER: {{ font_tier }}
{% if layout_hint %}

LAYOUT INTENT - which regions carry weight and how the components relate
(e.g. "chart is primary, table is supporting context beside it"). This is a
priority statement, NOT pixel coordinates: turn it into bands + a %/max split
using the LAYOUT GRAMMAR. If it conflicts with the grammar's rules, the grammar wins.
{{ layout_hint }}
{% endif %}
{% if supplied_content %}

SUPPLIED CONTENT (use these values EXACTLY, verbatim):
{% for key, value in supplied_content.items() %}
{{ key }}: {{ value }}
{% endfor %}
{% elif content_data %}

SLIDE-LEVEL DATA (fallback — use per-component data above when available):
{% for key, value in content_data.items() %}
{{ key }}: {{ value }}
{% endfor %}

For any component with no matching key above, invent realistic, specific
content - real-sounding numbers ($42.8M, 114%, +18% QoQ), named entities,
concise prose. Never "XX%", "TBD", "Lorem ipsum", "Company A", "Metric 1".
{% else %}

CONTENT: No data supplied - invent realistic, specific figures and text.
Real-sounding numbers ($42.8M, 114%, +18% QoQ), named entities, concise prose.
Never "XX%", "TBD", "Lorem ipsum", "Company A", "Metric 1". Every value should
look like it came from a real business report.
{% endif %}

HEIGHT BUDGET — follow the HEIGHT BUDGET section in the layout grammar.
RIGID bands (containing Chart/Table/Matrix/ProcessArrow/Flow/Pyramid/Tree/
Timeline) get explicit pixel h from the budget. TEXT-ONLY bands (callout,
narrative, bullet_list, kpi_row) get NO h — they auto-size to content.
KEEP TEXT SHORT so auto-sized bands stay ≤ ~150px each:
  Bullets: 1 line each (~50-60 chars). Callout body: 1 sentence (≤ 80 chars).
  Timeline description: 1-3 words ONLY — sentences collide in columns.
Weight tags apply to rigid bands' share of available_h only.
If the content is thin, add substance rather than leaving the slide half-empty.

Output the POM XML for this slide - a single <Slide> element, no <Theme>, no
markdown fences, no commentary.
